{
	title: 'ask tool: real models ask the user with a form',
	spec: 'Real models receive an ask tool for durable user questions, with question text and optional text, choice (options), and confirm fields; a missing fields list means one text answer. Models cannot request secret fields, and invalid model input becomes a tool error without parking. The tool description says to ask only for choices requiring the user and never for things the model can find out itself. A question uses the same session form block as synthetic models and commands: a turn parks without waiting in memory, survives a restart, shows attention and blocked (question), and the first answer resumes its call with plain text lines (name: Dave), preserving the order of other calls in the batch. Escape declines the question, returning a declined tool result without pausing the turn. Test the answer, restart, cancellation, secret rejection, and multiple calls.',
	status: 'done',
	needs: [
		'w4'
	],
	notes: [
		'src/host/tools/ask.ts provides form conversion and validates model input before parking; turns.ts checks pending calls before running them, reuses existing question and answer records on restart, and tools.run supplies the call id so a result reads only its own answer. Existing approval.held preserves a whole tool batch across questions. turn-recovery.ts was split from turns.ts to keep it under 400 lines.',
		'Tool call ids can repeat in later provider rounds. Scope answer lookup to the latest matching assistant tool call (ask.pending), not every question with the same id in the session.'
	]
}
